{
 "id": "rope-pulley-608-petg",
 "batch": 4,
 "brief": "A 60 mm rope pulley for a garage hoist, PETG on FDM, printed flat (layers along Z, the pulley's axis). It turns on a 608 bearing (22 mm OD, 7 mm wide) pressed into its hub from the top; the wheel is 60 mm across and 10 mm thick, z = -5 to 5, centred on the origin. The bearing seat runs from z = -3.5 up through the top, with a 1.5 mm lip under it and an 18 mm hole through the lip for the axle bolt and inner race. The 6 mm rope runs in a groove 6 mm wide (z = -3 to 3) whose floor is at r = 25; the groove's side flanges (r = 25 to 30) and a 1.5 mm floor under the rope must stay solid. The rope wraps half way round and both ends hang down (-Y): it lifts 15 kg, with a 2 g jerk, so each end pulls 294 N and the wheel takes 588 N down through the bottom of the groove; the rope can lead off up to 10 degrees out of the wheel's plane. Safety factor 2.",
